    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can provide personalized feedback and explain concepts in different ways. They can adapt to a student’s pace and style. They can also generate practice problems on the fly and offer hints. This helps students feel supported and less afraid of making mistakes. They're not replacements for teachers, but helpful tools that extend learning beyond the classroom."
